  "expected_answer": "Brief saved, state written, brand set; the line stops at keys: EXA_API_KEY (and MODEL_API_KEY / RESEND_API_KEY unless reused from an app that already runs) must be typed by the operator at a hidden prompt: python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret EXA_API_KEY.",
  "final_text": "I've set up Harbor Desk. It's stopped at the first step that needs you: its service keys.\n\n**What's done**\n- The brief is saved in `briefs/harbor_desk.md`, and the app's settings files are written and pass validation.\n- Branding is applied: Harbor Desk, colour #0B6E4F.\n- The deploy settings have web search on and browser off, as the brief asked.\n- Nothing has been deployed or tested yet.\n\n**What's stopping it**\nThe app needs 7 service keys that only you have. The usual shortcut, copying them from beta_app (which is already running), didn't work. This machine refuses to save a running app's keys to disk, so the copy failed. I checked and it left no key files behind. That means each key has to be entered by hand, one at a time.\n\n**The first one I need: your Cloudflare account ID.** The app uses Cloudflare to run its AI agents. It takes about 2 minutes:\n\n1. Open a **second terminal window** on this factory machine. Don't use this chat, so the value stays out of the conversation.\n2. Go to the factory folder and run:\n   ```\n   python3 .claude/scripts/provision.py harbor_desk --set-secret CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\n   ```\n3. It tells you where to find the value in Cloudflare, then asks you to paste it. What you paste stays hidden, and it isn't written to any file here or shown in the chat.\n4. Come back and tell me \"done\".\n\nAfter that, the other keys are entered the same way: the Cloudflare API token, the Resend email key, the address the app's emails come from, the Exa web-search key, and the Google sign-in ID. Once they're all in, the deploy is next. It takes about 10 minutes and creates the Vercel projects, a free database and file storage. I'll check with you before starting it.",
  "agent_error": false,
